    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter opening a file and doing `:restart` twice, I get `:badd` with no argument error and I also lose my buffer.\n```\nError in UIEnter Autocommands for \"*\":\nE5108: Lua: [string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:490: UIEnter Autocommands for \"*\"..script nvim_exec2() called at UIEnter Autocommands for \"*\":0[1]../tmp/nvim.nathan/restart_session_i\nivAnv, line 13: Vim(badd):E471: Argument required: badd +1\nstack traceback:\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'\n        [string \"vim/_core/editor\"]:490: in function 'cmd'\n        [string \":lua\"]:1: in main chunk\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `cd` to this repo\n2. `nvim . --clean`\n3. Use the browser to go open a file, e.g. `.clang-format`\n4. Type `:restart` twice\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI think this is happening because `:badd` from the first restart doesn't trigger the dir `BufEnter` autocommands, so stuff gets messed up. And then errors come up on the second restart.\n\nWilling to help on this, but not sure what to fix and whether the problem should be addressed from the dir side or restart side.\n\n\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1103+ge4137a7324\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nlinux mint 22.3\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nghostty 1.3.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nrepo build",
